[h1]Life Framework: Playtest Town[/h1]

Life Framework is an open-source roleplay framework for Arma Reforger. This item is its playtest build: one small 1989 Everon village where every system we have built so far runs side by side. It is unfinished. You will find rough edges, placeholder props and things that change between versions.

[h2]How to play[/h2]
[list]
[*]Subscribe to this item.
[*]Solo: open [b]Scenarios[/b], pick [b]Life Framework: Playtest Town[/b] and press Play.
[*]With friends: one of you hosts it from the Scenarios list, or joins a server that runs it. Server hosts: the config file and the host guide are linked below.
[/list]
No other mods are needed.

[h2]What to try[/h2]
[list]
[*]Fill in form R-89 when you arrive, then talk to the clerk on the square for your ID card.
[*]Take the parcel job at the depot. Fuel delivery and the taxi open as you level up.
[*]Bank your pay at the ATM and buy food at the general store.
[*]Collect your car from the garage, get the other one out of the impound, or buy one at the car lot.
[*]Rob a till, drill the bank vault or the cash van, and see the police get the call.
[*]Clock in at the police desk, work the wanted board, fine and jail.
[*]Get hurt and wait for the medic, or give up and respawn.
[*]Found an organization, use the hideout stash, sell to the fence, and run the moonshine still.
[/list]

[h2]Playtest settings[/h2]
[list]
[*]Your cash and bank top up when they run low, so you can try everything without grinding.
[*]Every new character owns two test cars, one in the garage and one at the impound.
[*]The first player on a server with no police is put on the police roster.
[*]Progress is saved and carries over a server restart.
[/list]

[h2]Feedback[/h2]
Tell us what broke, what confused you and what you liked. One report per problem, with what you did, what you expected and what happened. Screenshots help.
[list]
[*]Discord: [url=https://discord.gg/MjMexJteqz]discord.gg/MjMexJteqz[/url]
